== mutation check (step 3)
bash outputs/mutate-cutover.sh <worktree>      (JOBS=6; 119 mutations; baseline 84/84 on the unmutated copy)
  first run 100 mutations: 88 caught, 12 survived -> 12 real gaps in the tests (token file mode, force push on assist/*, one IAM role, one lane, a read-only mirror account,
  the tag names, step 7, the step-2 guard, a deploy without a verification, rollback enabling a workflow that was off before the cut, the t3 fate, the default minimum of 10 commits)
  -> added the cases (no test weakened), then the runbook / pipeline-runbook mutations, then the rehearse --dry-run ones; second round of survivors (4 runbook / lane-land checks that
  matched elsewhere in the file) -> made the checks specific; two secret-redaction mutations were masked by a second layer (output redaction) -> combined into one mutation each
  final: outputs/mutation-run.txt   mutations: 119   caught: 119   not caught: 0

